# Project Instructions

## Commands
- Build Docker image: `docker compose build agent`
- Run one-shot task: `docker compose run --rm agent "your task here"`
- Run hub/team mode: `docker compose run --rm agent hub --agent-name cryptofarian-builder --console`
- Local test: `python -m pytest`
- Container test: `docker compose run --rm --entrypoint /bin/sh agent -lc 'python -m pip install --user pytest >/tmp/dev-install.log && python -m pytest'`
- Lint: `ruff check .`
- Container lint: `docker compose run --rm --entrypoint /bin/sh agent -lc 'python -m pip install --user ruff >/tmp/dev-install.log && /tmp/.local/bin/ruff check .'`
- Syntax check: `python -m compileall src tests`

## Code Style
- Python 3.12+ with full type hints.
- Keep imports formatted with Ruff (`I`, `E`, `F`, `UP`, `B`, `SIM` are enabled).
- Store agent prompts as Jinja2 templates in `prompts/agents/`; do not hardcode system prompts in Python.
- Keep hub passwords and OpenRouter keys in `.env` or environment variables only.

## Workflow
- Run lint and tests before committing
- Write descriptive commit messages in imperative mood
- Create feature branches, never commit directly to main
- Do not perform live RunPod hub tests unless explicitly approved; hub posts are visible to the group and capped.
- Do not edit plan files in `/home/cryptofarian/.cursor/plans/` unless the user explicitly asks.

## Architecture
- Package code lives in `src/react_agent_system/`.
- `src/react_agent_system/agents.py` builds the LangGraph ReAct agent system.
- `src/react_agent_system/tools/` contains repository, research, bash, and agent-wrapper tools.
- `src/react_agent_system/hub/` contains RunPod hub team mode: client, limiter, budget, assessment, console, and loop.
- `prompts/agents/` contains Jinja2 prompt templates for all agent roles.
- `config/agents.example.yaml` and `.env.example` document runtime configuration.
- `compose.yaml` runs the CLI container with the repo mounted at `/workspace`.

## Platform / Environment
- Runtime: Python 3.12+
- Package metadata: `pyproject.toml`
- Container runtime: Docker Compose service `agent`
- LLM provider: OpenRouter via LangChain OpenAI-compatible chat model
- Session persistence: SQLite checkpointer under `sessions/`

## Gotchas
- Host Python may not have `pip`, `pytest`, `ruff`, or `uv`; use containerized test/lint commands when needed.
- `docker compose run --rm agent ...` uses the image entrypoint `react-agent`.
- For shell access in the slim Python image, use `/bin/sh`, not `/bin/bash`.
- The repo is bind-mounted into the container at `/workspace`; file writes there affect the host repo.
- Hub mode requires `REACT_AGENT_HUB_PASSWORD`; one-shot task mode requires `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.
- Hub mode must assess relevance before responding; agents must not auto-reply to every group message.
